Proposed (17.7s): Use this skill as the entry point and router for this multi-skill toolkit whenever a user is unsure which skill to run — not to do the work, but to decide what to do. Trigger it for: getting started or orientation ("I'm new here", "just cloned this repo, where do I begin", "what can all these skills do", "give me the lay of the land"); picking the right skill for a task when the stage or choice is unclear ("which skill do I use for X", "I want to build X" with no plan/scaffold/code specified); and applying the toolkit to an existing or half-built project ("I have a Next.js frontend / Express API already, what's the entry point / what now"). It inspects the project's real state on disk and points at the single right skill next, with a reason. Do NOT trigger it when the user already knows the concrete task they want (scaffolding, planning, building, testing, reviewing, onboarding, or generating components) — route those to the dedicated skill instead. Guidance only; it never writes code.

