  "original_description": "The front desk of this skill toolkit \u2014 inspects the current project's real state and tells the user exactly which skill to run next and why. Use this whenever the user is unsure where to begin or what comes next: \"where do I start\", \"what should I do next\", \"which skill do I use for this\", \"I'm new to this toolkit\", \"help me get started\", \"guide me\", \"what can these skills do\", \"I have an existing project, now what\". Also use it when a request is real but ambiguous about stage \u2014 \"I want to build X\" without saying plan vs scaffold vs code \u2014 so the user gets routed instead of a random skill mis-firing. It reads .claude/workspace.json, the ARCHITECTURE.md / MODULE_REGISTRY.md contract files, any _docs/prd/PRD.md and _docs/**/FEATURE_PLAN_*.md, and follows LAYOUT.md's resolution protocol + NAMING.md's taxonomy so its routing always matches the installed skills. It is guidance ONLY \u2014 it diagnoses state and hands off with a clear next step; it never scaffolds, onboards, plans, builds, tests, reviews, or writes any project code itself (those are the dedicated skills it points at). Not for doing the work \u2014 only for deciding which worker skill does it.",
